diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ff92be649ff3f610b38798b3310751534d032814..e6bfbeeb8207b64fdd728385f6ad50db46b10d31 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves an [RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)
+and returns the selected value. It throws when the pointer is malformed or does not select a value.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ users: [{ name: "Ada" }] }, "/users/0/name"); // "Ada"
+```
diff --git a/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-token-traversal.md b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-token-traversal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cb6c95e3f5ed471953b8dfcec78465ef7fc4d8d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-token-traversal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-token-traversal
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use strict RFC 6901 token traversal"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need a single resolver for JSON Pointer values. RFC 6901 defines both
+the pointer syntax and how reference tokens select object members and array
+elements.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate that a pointer is either empty or begins with `/`; decode reference
+tokens only through the RFC escape sequences (`~0` and `~1`); and traverse only
+own object properties and canonical JSON array indices. Treat every malformed
+pointer or missing traversal target as an error.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The resolver does not silently accept malformed escapes, inherited properties,
+array append token `-`, or non-canonical array indices. Callers get a clear
+failure instead of an ambiguous or unsafe result.
